|issn=0016-0318
|lccn=73643417
|oclc=1786626
|location=Taipei
|page=1
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_free-china-weekly_1973-10-21_14_41/
|column=1
|text=Premier Chiang Ching-kuo said October 12 that the {{w|National Freeway 1|North-South Freeway}}, a 373-kilometer (235-mile) '''artery''' along west Taiwan, will have to be completed on schedule by 1978.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 May 6|author=Graeme Pickering|title=Borders Railway: time for the next step|journal=[[w:Rail (magazine)|Rail]]|url=https://www.railmagazine.com|page=52|text=The 98-mile Edinburgh-Carlisle 'Waverley Route' provided over a century of service as an Anglo-Scottish '''artery''', prior to its closure by British Rail, and its loss provoked anger in the [[Scottish Borders]].}}

