===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|anelen}}, {{m|enm|onelen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|onǣlan||to [[burn#Verb|burn]], [[ignite]], [[set fire]] to, [[consume]], [[heat#Verb|heat]], [[enlighten]], [[incite]], [[inflame]], [[inspire]], [[kindle]]}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*ana||on}} + {{der|en|gem-pro|*ailijaną||to burn}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂eydʰ-||to burn}}. The double-N spelling may have arisen by analogy with Latinate verbs like {{m|en|announce}}, {{m|en|annex}}, and {{m|en|annul}}.

The word is related to {{cog|ang|onāl||that which is [[burnt]], [[burning#Noun|burning]]; [[incense]]}}, {{cog|ang|āl||[[fire]], burning}}, {{cog|is|eldur||fire}}, {{cog|sv|eld||fire, [[flame#Noun|flame]]}}, {{cog|da|ild||fire}}.

