===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:bor|fr:archive<id:noun>|tree=1}}
The {{lg|noun}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|archive}}, {{m|fr|archif}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|archīvum}}, {{m|la-lat|archīum|t=archive; room containing an archive; public record office}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀρχεῖον|t=office of a magistrate; public building or office; town hall; (''in the plural'') archives; public records}}, a noun use of the {{lg|neuter}} form of {{m|grc|*ἀρχεῖος|t=relating to an office}}, from {{m|grc|ᾰ̓ρχή|t=beginning, origin; authority, sovereignty}} (from {{m|grc|ἄρχω|t=to begin; to govern, rule}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8587287968|date=March 2026|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220123030917/https://www.lexico.com/definition/archive}}</ref> further etymology uncertain, possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂er-|t=to fit; to fix; to put together}}, or {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ergʰ-|t=to begin; to command; to rule}}) + {{m|grc|-ῐος|pos={{lg|suffix}} meaning ‘of or relating to’ forming {{lg|adjective}}s}}.

The {{lg|verb}} is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9354017580|date=December 2025|nodot=}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220123030917/https://www.lexico.com/definition/archive}}</ref>

