#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2009/jan/13/spain-art|title=Google Earth brings masterpieces from Prado museum direct to armchair art lovers|date=2009-01-13|author=w:Giles Tremlett|work=w:The Guardian|passage='''Armchair''' tourists who are used to travelling the globe with Google Earth can now use the same technology to crawl all over the masterpieces in one of the world's most famous galleries: the Prado.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210415011318/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2009/jan/13/spain-art}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/drones-ethics-and-the-armchair-soldier/|title=Drones, Ethics and the Armchair Soldier|date=2013-03-17|author=John Kaag|work=''The [[w:New York Times|New York Times]]'' Opinionator|passage=My point here is not that these new '''armchair''' soldiers are to be criticized for failing in their moral responsibilities. My point is rather that while drones are to be applauded for keeping these soldiers out of harm’s way physically, we would do well to remember that they do not keep them out of harm’s way morally or psychologically.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250210153205/https://archive.nytimes.com/opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/drones-ethics-and-the-armchair-soldier/}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Bridget Christie|url=http://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2015/apr/11/bridget-christie-armchair-activist|title=We’re a nation of armchair activists – what’s wrong with that?|date=2015-04-11|work=w:The Guardian|passage=E-petitions have turned us all into '''armchair''' activists, and there’s nothing wrong with that.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170701133946/https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2015/apr/11/bridget-christie-armchair-activist}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michael Schwirtz; Ellen Barry|title=Armchair Investigators at Front of British Inquiry Into Spy Poisoning|work=w:The New York Times|date=2018-10-09|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/09/world/europe/bellingcat-skripal-poisoning.html|issn=0362-4331|passage='''Armchair''' Investigators at Front of British Inquiry Into Spy Poisoning [title]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210206225641/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/09/world/europe/bellingcat-skripal-poisoning.html}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|derogatory}} {{U|unqualified}} or [[uninformed]] but yet giving [[advice]], especially on technical issues, such as law, architecture, medicine, military theory, or sports; relating to such advice.
