#: {{ux|en|After the game, the [[armchair quarterback|'''armchair''' quarterback]]s talked about what they would have done differently to win.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Patrick D. Healy|title=Gay Republicans Soldier On, One Skirmish at a Time|work=w:The New York Times|date=2005-04-17|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2005/04/17/weekinreview/gay-republicans-soldier-on-one-skirmish-at-a-time.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=If and when Ms. Cheney decides to marry, it will be interesting to see who offers best wishes, who offers '''armchair''' psychoanalysis, and who minds his own business.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210818082156/https://www.nytimes.com/2005/04/17/weekinreview/gay-republicans-soldier-on-one-skirmish-at-a-time.html}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2024-10-10|author=|work=w:Australian Broadcasting Corporation|title=New Zealand defence minister says a navy ship didn't sink because its captain was a woman|url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-10-11/new-zealand-defence-minister-hits-out-sexist-trolling-of-navy/104459964|text={{w|Judith Collins}}, who is New Zealand's first female defence minister, said she was appalled to see a "deeply concerning [[misogynistic]] narrative" online from "'''armchair''' admirals, people who will never have to make decisions which mean life or death for their subordinates".|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241224094800/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-10-11/new-zealand-defence-minister-hits-out-sexist-trolling-of-navy/104459964}}

